                    <h3>What is Term Insurance?</h3>
                    <p>
                        Term Insurance is a life insurance plan that provides financial protection for a specific period. If the insured person passes away during the policy term, the policy may provide a death benefit to the nominee, subject to the policy terms and conditions.
                    </p>

                    <ul>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Provides financial protection for your family.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Offers life cover for a selected policy period.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Can help support family expenses and financial responsibilities.</span></li>
                        <li><i class="bi bi-check-circle"></i> <span>Can be considered as part of a long-term financial protection plan.</span></li>
                    </ul>

                    <p>
                        Term Insurance can be useful for individuals who have financial responsibilities such as household expenses, loans, children's education, or other future financial commitments. The required life cover depends on income, responsibilities, existing savings, liabilities, and financial goals.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Before choosing a Term Insurance plan, consider the coverage amount, policy term, premium, eligibility, exclusions, nominee details, claim conditions, and other policy terms. Benefits and conditions may vary depending on the selected insurance product and the applicable policy terms.
